 can you help the Essex horse and pony  protection society eh PPS with its  winter hay appeal because the sanctuary  is located on a site of special  scientific interest grazing is severely  restricted between october and april  every year the horses and ponies they  rescue chomp their way through 30 bales  of hay a day that's 210 bales a week  which costs over 1,000 pounds they need  contributions to help them behave the  ponies and horses they rescue for more  details on how you can help contact 0126  858 4603 or email administrator at eh  PPS org dot uk' can you foster cats with  the cold weather coming we look forward  to living in warm houses but life is  tough for many stray cats during the  summer a lot of stray cats are fine  people are happy to feed them and watch  them laze around in their gardens but  that all changes come the winter  Rayleigh cats protection urgently need  to get these cats into a safe warm and  secure place so they don't have to eat  frozen food shiver in the cold and get  soaked in the rain they desperately need  your help could you become one of their  foster errs they'll provide food cat  litter bowls and pay any veterinary  costs you just need a spare room and  time to give them a care and attention  for homing information call 0126 8750  8314 fostering 0126 879 4648 or visit w  wh org UK  or could you help abandoned dogs in the  district the Friends of abandoned dogs  at acres way are also always looking for  homes for the many abandoned dogs in  their care and whatever the time of year  the dogs they care for still need  feeding the kennels are always very  grateful for any donations from members  of the public of dog food or treats to  help feed their charges especially over  the Christmas period they would also  welcome any donations of blankets or  towels to keep the dogs warm and dry  during the damp wintery days if you're  interested in finding out more or  helping the Friends of abandoned dogs  you can contact the kennels on 01 268  double 7040 to you can also take your  donations direct to then at acres way  kennels great birches Road thundersley  rochford score strategy inspector says  plan for the district's future is sound  watch the district councils plan for the  future development of the district the  poor strategy has been approved by the  government inspector conducting the  examination the core strategy sets out  the key planning policies for the  district and will determine how the area  will develop over the next 15 years and  beyond it addresses issues such as the  location and type of new housing sites  for employment development strategic  infrastructure requirements and town  center in Harmons nents to name but a  few it also introduces a number of  measures to ensure the protection of the  district's environment following  extensive community involvement  appraisal and evidence gathering the  council's of greed core strategy was  submitted to the government for  examination in January 2010 to determine  whether the strategy was sound and  legally compliant the council had  expected the results of the examination  to be issued within six months the usual  time for the government to consider such  plans however as a result of the change  in government amendments to national  policy and legal challenges against the  secretary of state for communities and  local government the examination process  was significantly delayed the planning  inspectorate has now issued its report  on the core strategy and found it to be  sound the core strategy ensures the vast  majority of the district's greenbelt is  protected from development directing  housing and employment to the most  appropriate locations it will also  ensure new development is built to high  environmental standards meets the needs  of the local community and is  accompanied by Lana the cloth strategy  covers a diverse range of issues from  protecting environmentally sensitive  areas and providing new recreational  spaces to setting out framework for  economic growth in the district  including tell centre enhancements and  development around london Southend  Airport  the inspectors report will be presented  to the council on the 13th of december  for consideration and subject to  approval by the council formal adoption  adoption of the core strategy will mean  locations for future development are  confirmed the council is now progressing  work on related policy documents this  will include the allocations development  plan document which will set out the  precise boundaries of the sites to be  developed within the general locations  now confirmed by the core strategy and  the development management development  plan document which will provide  detailed policies events to which  planning applications will be determined  look for opportunities to have your say  on these in the new year for further  details interview information on the  core strategy visit our website w WAW k  as the days get shorter and the weather  gets colder the council has put together  a few handy heads about how you and your  family can prepare for winter protect  your home check that pipes are  adequately lagged check that you've  ordered your winter heating fuel check  that you know where your stop tap is  located find out if you're entitled to  grants and subsidies for home heating  and insulation traveling before you  travel check the winter weather forecast  at the Met Office's winter weather  portal check that your vehicle is ready  for winter check that you know where to  find traffic and travel information  check local and national weather  forecasts and keep up to date with the  latest warnings technically have an  emergency kit available in your car  communities check that you know who  might need helping your community area  in really bad weather sign up for  weather warnings on the Met Office  website and check whether you're at risk  of flooding and sign up for free flood  warnings by visiting the environment  agency's website and here are some  useful websites for you ww-what org dot  uk' ww directgov UK www Met Office gov  UK www environment hyphen agency dot-gov  UK and www 6 govt UK forward slash  winter and don't forget to get the jab  that could save your life it's the time  of year when we see many people  suffering from flu-like illness like  every winter the flu viruses circulate  and attack people with a weak immune  system and those suffering from other  long-term conditions like asthma and  diabetes nationally during the 2009  winter season more people died from  influenza and pneumonia than those who  died with breast or prostate cancer  the NHS in south essex is urging people  at risk of flu to get protected and have  the vaccine for groups have been  identified as being most at-risk  pregnant women people with long-term  conditions and serious illness that make  their immune system weak for example  cancer asthma diabetes heart disease and  neurological illnesses carers who look  after vulnerable people and people over  65 years the head of public health for  NHS southeast Essex Margaret Gray said  flu is different from getting a cold and  the effects of seasonal flu are often  underestimated some people at more at  risk from flu and need the vaccine  because they're not able to fight off  flu as easily as others it can often  result in more serious complications  which require hospital treatment and the  figures from last winter show that  sometimes there can be devastating  consequences of death this can be  prevented by having the vaccine which is  being provided free to eligible people  at GP surgeries across south essex for  people with long term conditions carers  those over 65 and pregnant women  associate director of public health at  NHS south west essex dr. aaron patel  added flu is a highly infectious illness  caused by viruses we now have a safe  effective vaccine vaccine for the  viruses that will circulate this winter  it's important that those at risk  protect themselves every year and  getting the free job helps protect them  and their loved ones there are  additional ways people can protect  themselves and those around them good  hand hygiene they catch it vinit kill it  technique reduces the spread of germs  this means carrying tissues covering  coughs and sneezes with a tissue  disposing of the tissue after one use  and cleaning hands as soon as possible  with soap and water or an alcohol hand  gel people in the at-risk groups can get  their free flu vaccine by contacting  their  GP practice for more information visit  www.pay
 

